# Double multiplication with integer operands

Multiplies 7 by 2.25 in both operand orders to verify the integer is
promoted and the result stays a double, producing 15.75 either way.

>>> source
integer_left: int = 7
double_value: double = 2.25

// Verifies the Int-to-Double promotion.
integer_times_double: double = integer_left * double_value
print(integer_times_double)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
double_times_integer: double = double_value * integer_left
print(double_times_integer)

<<< stdout
15.75
15.75

<<< stderr
